The plate holds two corn cob segments, each about 4 cm across and 3–4 cm long. Each is roughly 50–60 g with the cob, so the total is about 110 g.

Corn on the cob has about 0.9 kcal/g including the cob. Kernels alone are about 1.0 kcal/g, and the cob adds mass with few calories. That gives roughly 100 kcal for the two pieces.

